gions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports as verified, with every region on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy, and v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. Because v2.3.0 has already been healthy in production, the change-manager approval policy didn't apply.\n- **Before the rollback:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1, unhealthy, with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api. It paged on-call and describes the rollback and the release history.\n\nI haven't rechecked the error rate since the rollback, so recovery is not yet confirmed. The incident lists confirming recovery and investigating the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing as follow-ups.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Wb6pz8Bbyh85HjrrAUf1eK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M1KycNmhVcQ2YQ5iY28F4c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 has been healthy in production, so the change-manager approval policy doesn't apply. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017VS6rRLPEiJngg98YuBNJe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XkpKhXEYWLUU1kYw1MpYJU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate was 0.18). Release history: v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports VERIFIED and all regions are on v2.3.0. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports as verified, with every region on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy, and v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. Because v2.3.0 has already been healthy in production, the change-manager approval policy didn't apply.\n- **Before the rollback:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1, unhealthy, with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api. It paged on-call and describes the rollback and the release history.\n\nI haven't rechecked the error rate since the rollback, so recovery is not yet confirmed. The incident lists confirming recovery and investigating the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing as follow-ups.", "type": "text"}]}]}